        {id: "s13", label: "13. Related Standards"},
        {id: "s14", label: "14. Glossary"}
    ]} />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">

<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A deliberate convergence move — bringing J-GAAP into line with IAS 2</div><div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 9 governs the MEASUREMENT of inventories (棚卸資産) — the COST formulas an entity may use, and the requirement to write inventories DOWN when their value has genuinely DECLINED below cost. A NOTABLE feature of this Statement is that its DEVELOPMENT specifically ELIMINATED the LAST-IN, FIRST-OUT (LIFO) cost formula from acceptable J-GAAP practice — a DELIBERATE convergence move aligning Japanese practice with IAS 2's LONG-STANDING prohibition of LIFO internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">All companies holding inventories</div><div class="principle">This Statement applies to ALL companies holding inventories — merchandise, finished goods, work in progress, raw materials, and supplies — held for SALE in the ordinary course of business or CONSUMPTION in producing goods or services for sale.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Lower of Cost and Net Realisable Value</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">The core measurement principle</div><div class="text-supporting">Inventories are measured at the LOWER of their determined COST and NET REALISABLE VALUE (正味売却価額, "net selling value") — where an item's net realisable value has FALLEN below its recorded cost, the carrying amount must be WRITTEN DOWN to reflect the LOWER, currently-recoverable amount, consistent with the general principle that assets should NOT be carried above their recoverable economic value.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Acceptable Cost Formulas — and the Elimination of LIFO</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">FIFO, weighted average, and specific identification — LIFO no longer permitted</div><div class="text-supporting">Acceptable cost formulas under this Statement include FIRST-IN, FIRST-OUT (FIFO), WEIGHTED AVERAGE cost, and SPECIFIC IDENTIFICATION for uniquely identifiable items. LAST-IN, FIRST-OUT (LIFO) — historically PERMITTED under EARLIER Japanese practice — was SPECIFICALLY ELIMINATED as an acceptable cost formula through this Statement's development, a deliberate step bringing J-GAAP INTO ALIGNMENT with IAS 2, which has LONG PROHIBITED LIFO internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Write-Down to Net Realisable Value — Presentation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Generally within cost of sales, unless the decline is unusual in nature or scale</div><div class="text-supporting">A write-down to net realisable value is generally presented WITHIN cost of sales — reflecting the ORDINARY, recurring nature of typical inventory valuation declines. Where the DECLINE is UNUSUAL in nature or SIGNIFICANT in scale (e.g. reflecting a natural disaster or an extraordinary market disruption), it may instead be presented as a SEPARATE, distinctly labelled loss.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Reversal of Write-Downs</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Permitted where net realisable value subsequently recovers</div><div class="text-supporting">Where an item's NET REALISABLE VALUE subsequently RECOVERS in a LATER period (after a previous write-down), the write-down may be REVERSED — but ONLY up to the ORIGINAL cost figure, NEVER above it — consistent with IAS 2's own reversal requirement, and reflecting that the write-down was always intended to capture a genuine, though not necessarily PERMANENT, decline in value.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Worked Example — a Write-Down to Net Realisable Value</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Writing inventory down to its recoverable amount</div>
<div class="worked worked--flush"><div class="wk-title">Example: Obsolete finished goods inventory</div><div class="wk-body">A company holds finished goods inventory with a recorded cost of ¥60,000,000. Due to a sudden shift in market demand, the estimated net realisable value has fallen to ¥45,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company writes the inventory DOWN by ¥15,000,000 (¥60,000,000 − ¥45,000,000), recognising the amount generally WITHIN cost of sales, bringing the carrying amount to <strong>¥45,000,000</strong> — reflecting the LOWER of cost and net realisable value.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Reversal of a Prior Write-Down</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Recovering value, capped at original cost</div>
<div class="worked worked--flush"><div class="wk-title">Example: Demand recovers in a later period</div><div class="wk-body">Continuing the prior example, market demand RECOVERS in the following period, and the SAME inventory's net realisable value rises back to ¥58,000,000 (still below the original ¥60,000,000 cost).</div><div class="wk-answer">The company REVERSES ¥13,000,000 of the prior write-down (¥58,000,000 − ¥45,000,000), bringing the carrying amount up to <strong>¥58,000,000</strong> — but NOT above the ORIGINAL ¥60,000,000 cost, even if net realisable value were to recover further still.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 9 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Accounting policy for inventory cost formula and measurement basis</span><span>Amount of inventories carried at net realisable value, and write-downs recognised during the period</span><span>Amount of any reversal of previous write-downs recognised during the period</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether an inventory value decline is ordinary/recurring versus unusual, affecting presentation</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Estimated net realisable value, based on expected selling price less estimated costs to complete and sell</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS — and the Contrast With US GAAP</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison across all three major frameworks</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-1-1-1"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 9)</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS (IAS 2) / US GAAP</span></div>
<div class="tr cols-1-1-1"><span>LIFO permitted</span><span>NO — eliminated</span><span>IFRS: NO (never permitted). US GAAP: YES — LIFO remains permitted</span></div>
<div class="tr alt cols-1-1-1"><span>Reversal of write-downs</span><span>PERMITTED, capped at original cost</span><span>IFRS: PERMITTED, capped at original cost — converged. US GAAP: NOT permitted once written down</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">Japan's elimination of LIFO was a DELIBERATE step TOWARD IFRS, moving AWAY from where US GAAP still stands — one of the clearer examples of J-GAAP choosing IFRS convergence over alignment with US practice on a SPECIFIC measurement question.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every inventory measurement event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Write-down to net realisable value</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Generally within cost of sales</span></div>
<div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Reversal of a prior write-down</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Capped at original cost</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 29</span><span>Revenue Recognition — governs when inventory sales are recognised, working alongside this Statement's measurement principles</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Net realisable value (正味売却価額)</div><div class="glossary-def">Estimated selling price less estimated costs to complete and sell, the ceiling used alongside cost for the lower-of measurement.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last"><div class="glossary-term">LIFO (Last-In, First-Out) — eliminated</div><div class="glossary-def">A cost formula historically permitted under earlier Japanese practice, removed from acceptable use as part of this Statement's convergence with IAS 2.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表) <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書) <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部 <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書) <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</div></div>

  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
